    "id": "p10-q17-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "Draw a diagram and prove that if each angle of a quadrilateral is equal to the opposite angle then the quadrilateral is a parallelogram.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Both pairs of opposite sides are parallel, so the quadrilateral is a parallelogram.",
      "worked": "Label the quadrilateral ABCD in order. Let $\\angle A=\\angle C=\\alpha$ and $\\angle B=\\angle D=\\beta$. Its angle sum gives $2\\alpha+2\\beta=360^\\circ$, so $\\alpha+\\beta=180^\\circ$. Therefore $\\angle BAD+\\angle ABC=180^\\circ$, giving $AD\\parallel BC$ by the converse co-interior-angle property. Also $\\angle ABC+\\angle BCD=180^\\circ$, giving $AB\\parallel CD$. Both pairs of opposite sides are parallel, so ABCD is a parallelogram.",
